  "summary": "The previous proposal correctly identifies the root cause (getKey() trapped inside {{if .ShowKeyModal}} blocks) but its suggested fix of replacing getKey() calls with _dashKey has a critical gap: _dashKey only exists in client.html (line 497), not in index.html. In index.html, the edit functions (saveEditTitle, saveEditType, saveEditDescription, saveEditDoneScript at lines 763/804/842/900) call getKey() but are inside the {{if .Authenticated}} block where a different global variable `key` (line 386, defined via IIFE) is already available. So the fix must be different per file: use _dashKey in client.html, and use the existing `key` variable in index.html. Additionally, the proposal overlooks that logout() and restartClient() (index.html lines 1090-1111) are also trapped inside the ShowKeyModal block — logout() is called at line 301 from the Authenticated block but defined at line 1090 inside ShowKeyModal; there IS a duplicate logout() at line 455 inside the Authenticated block that would take precedence for the dashboard page, but restartClient() has no such duplicate and would also fail. The cleanest fix is to move getKey() out of the ShowKeyModal conditional in both files so it's always defined, rather than replacing calls site-by-site, since that approach also fixes the restartClient issue in index.html and avoids inconsistent key-resolution strategies across the two files."
